  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "A cuboid has dimensions $a\\times b\\times c$. If each of these is increased by a factor of $2$, then by what factor does the surface area increase?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "A factor of $4$.",
      "worked": "The original surface area is $A=2ab+2ac+2bc$. After doubling each dimension,\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{new}}&=2(2a)(2b)+2(2a)(2c)+2(2b)(2c)\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=8ab+8ac+8bc\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=4(2ab+2ac+2bc)\\\\A_{\\text{new}}&=4A\\end{align*}$$\nThe surface area increases by a factor of $4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
